From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v8-embed-feedstock <noreply@github.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Run a Windows action's executable without the shell

gyp's ninja generator runs every action on Windows through gyp-win-tool's
action-wrapper, which hands the whole command to subprocess with
shell=True: one cmd.exe /c line.  cmd.exe reads at most 8191 characters
of it, and what comes after is silently gone.

run_torque is longer than that.  Its command names some 245 .tq files,
and with the absolute paths of a build tree in front it comes to about
8150 characters -- or more, depending on where the tree sits.  The
inputs at the end were dropped; among them src/objects/torque-defined-
classes.tq, which is where torque files the C++ definitions of every
class that has no hand-written header (ClassType::AttributedToFile).
With that source missing those definitions had nowhere to go: torque
wrote an empty torque-defined-classes-tq.inc, instance-types.h still
listed the classes, and the first translation unit to include
objects-body-descriptors-inl.h failed with "incomplete type
'StrongDescriptorArray' named in nested name specifier".  Node's own
Windows builds never see it: they run these actions through MSBuild.

When the command starts with an executable there is nothing for the
shell to do.  Passed as a string with shell=False, subprocess gives the
line to CreateProcess unchanged, which accepts up to 32767 characters.
Anything else -- a shell built-in, a batch file -- still goes through
cmd.exe as before.
---
 tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/win_tool.py | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/win_tool.py b/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/win_tool.py
--- a/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/win_tool.py
+++ b/tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/win_tool.py
@@ -352,6 +352,15 @@
                 env[k] = v
         args = open(rspfile).read()
         dir = dir[0] if dir else None
+        # Through the shell, this is one cmd.exe /c line, and cmd.exe stops
+        # reading at 8191 characters: what follows is silently gone.  An
+        # action that lists a few hundred input files -- torque, with V8's
+        # .tq sources -- is longer than that, and lost its last inputs.
+        # When the command starts with an executable, there is nothing for
+        # the shell to do; CreateProcess takes the line as it is, up to 32K.
+        first = args.split(None, 1)[0].strip('"') if args.strip() else ""
+        if first.lower().endswith(".exe") and os.path.isfile(first):
+            return subprocess.call(args, shell=False, env=env, cwd=dir)
         return subprocess.call(args, shell=True, env=env, cwd=dir)
 
     def ExecClCompile(self, project_dir, selected_files):
